[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Tutorial: GraphQL and WebSocket Request Handling in Postman"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Modern API architectures often move beyond traditional REST endpoints to support real-time data streaming and complex querying. GraphQL allows clients to request exact data structures, while WebSockets enable persistent, bidirectional communication channels. Postman provides robust native support for testing both GraphQL queries/mutations and WebSocket connections."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Part 1: Testing GraphQL APIs in Postman"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"GraphQL uses a single endpoint to handle queries (reading data) and mutations (writing data). Postman has a dedicated GraphQL request mode that automatically formats payloads and provides schema intellisense."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Open Postman and click the 'New' button, then select 'GraphQL Request'."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Enter your GraphQL endpoint URL into the request URL field (e.g., https://rickandmortyapi.com/graphql)."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Navigate to the 'Query' tab in the request builder interface."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"query GetCharacter {
  character(id: 1) {
    name
    status
    species
  }
}"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"If your query requires dynamic variables, you can define them in the 'GraphQL Variables' section below the query editor using valid JSON syntax:"},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"{
  "characterId": 2
}"},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Click 'Send' to execute the request and view the JSON response payload in the lower pane."},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"Part 2: Establishing and Testing WebSocket Connections"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"WebSockets maintain an open TCP connection between the client and server, allowing messages to flow instantly in both directions without HTTP overhead. Postman supports WebSocket requests natively."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Click 'New' in Postman and select 'WebSocket Request'."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Ensure the protocol dropdown is set to 'Raw WebSocket' (or use Socket.IO if your server implements it)."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Enter your WebSocket server URI (e.g., wss://echo.websocket.events) and click 'Connect'."},{"order":17,"type":"paragraph","text":"Once the connection status indicator turns green, you can send messages through the interactive message composer."},{"order":18,"type":"code","text":"{
  "action": "subscribe",
  "channel": "updates"
}"},{"order":19,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Click 'Send' to transmit the message over the active socket connection."},{"order":20,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Observe incoming server messages in the real-time event log timeline at the bottom of the Postman interface."},{"order":21,"type":"subheading","text":"Part 3: GraphQL Subscriptions over WebSockets"},{"order":22,"type":"paragraph","text":"GraphQL Subscriptions combine both concepts. They allow clients to listen for real-time events using GraphQL syntax over an underlying WebSocket transport layer (typically using protocols like 'graphql-transport-ws')."},{"order":23,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Create a new WebSocket Request in Postman pointing to your GraphQL subscription endpoint using the 'graphql-transport-ws' subprotocol."},{"order":24,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Initiate the connection and send the initialization payload required by the GraphQL ws protocol:"},{"order":25,"type":"code","text":"{
  "type": "connection_init"
}"},{"order":26,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Once acknowledged, send your subscription query payload:"},{"order":27,"type":"code","text":"{
  "id": "1",
  "type": "subscribe",
  "payload": {
    "query": "subscription OnNewMessage { messageAdded { id content } }"
  }
}"},{"order":28,"type":"paragraph","text":"You will now receive incremental data packets directly inside the Postman WebSocket message log whenever the server triggers the subscription event."}]
